>Klebsiella pneumoniae</italic> causing pyogenic liver abscesses: exact role in serotype K1 capsule formation</article-title><source>J Infect Dis</source><year>2010</year><volume>201</volume><fpage>1259</fpage><lpage>67</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">19785524</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R13"><label>13</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chou</surname><given-names>HC</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>CZ</given-names></name><name><surname>Ma</surname><given-names>LC</given-names></name><name><surname>Fang</surname><given-names>CT</given-names></name><name><surname>Chang</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>JT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Isolation of a chromosomal region of <italic>Klebsiella pneumoniae</italic> associated with allantoin metabolism and liver infection</article-title><source>Infect Immun</source><year>2004</year><volume>72</volume><fpage>3783</fpage><lpage>92</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15213119</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R14"><label>14</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fang</surname><given-names>CT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A novel virulence gene in <italic>Klebsiella pneumoniae</italic> strains causing primary liver abscess and septic metastatic complications</article-title><source>J Exp Med</source><year>2004</year><volume>199</volume><fpage>697</fpage><lpage>705</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14993253</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R15"><label>15</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tsai</surname><given-names>F-C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Pyogenic liver abscess as endemic disease, Taiwan</article-title><source>Emerging Infect Dis</source><year>2008</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>1592</fpage><lpage>600</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18826824</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R16"><label>16</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Struve</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Investigation of the putative virulence gene <italic>magA</italic> in a worldwide collection of 495 <italic>Klebsiella</italic> isolates: <italic>magA</italic> is restricted to the gene cluster of <italic>Klebsiella pneumoniae</italic> capsule serotype K1</article-title><source>J Med Microbiol</source><year>2005</year><volume>54</volume><fpage>1111</fpage><lpage>3</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16192445</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R17"><label>17</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hsieh</surname><given-names>PF</given-names></name><name><surname>Lin</surname><given-names>TL</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>CZ</given-names></name><name><surname>Tsai</surname><given-names>SF</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>JT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Serum-induced iron-acquisition systems and TonB contribute to virulence in <italic>Klebsiella pneumoniae</italic> causing primary pyogenic liver abscess</article-title><source>J Infect Dis</source><year>2008</year><volume>197</volume><fpage>1717</fpage><lpage>27</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18433330</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R18"><label>18</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Turton</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>Baklan</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Siu</surname><given-names>LK</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaufmann</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surna